# Huatli's Final Strike has two targets, both required: a creature you control and a creature an opponent controls (unlike Assert Perfection's "up to one"). Turn 3: Bot2 controls no
# creature, so the spell can't be cast although Bot1's Alpine Grizzly is there. On turn 5 Bot2's Ornithopter is a legal second target and the Strike is cast: a Mox Jet is no creature (the
# refusal), and Alpine Grizzly, 5/2 now, kills the Ornithopter (Bot2 also discarded an Island down to seven cards at turn 4's cleanup).

